Serialize every FFTW planner user with one global mutex (backport).

FFTW's planner (fftw_plan_*, fftw_destroy_plan) is not thread-safe; only
fftw_execute is. A preset with two convolvers (a surround impulse plus a
headphone correction) loads both kernels at the same instant, each on its
own worker thread, and the two ConvolverKernelFFT::compute_fft_magnitude
calls race inside the planner: SIGSEGV in fftw_execute,
fftw_plan_destroy_internal or fftw_mkplan_d within ~10 ms of
"Calculating the impulse fft..." (8 of 8 runs under gdb, easyeffects
8.0.5, 2026-10-12). Quitting or switching presets while a kernel loads
hits the same race.

Backport of upstream wwmm/easyeffects 95842279ab "Adding a global fftw
mutex" (2025-12-13; util::fftw_lock() held in the kernel FFT, in
ConvolverZita::init/process and in FirFilterBase) plus 3245d903d1 (the
complex_output buffer sized to the spectrum, not the signal). Adapted to
the 8.0.5 compute_fft_magnitude signature; std::scoped_lock as in eff2fea3e1.

